  <p>
    <strong>Digital currency markets have slid in value over the last 12 hours as the entire crypto-economy has lost over 7% during the last 24 hours. Bitcoin attempted to cross the $40k handle but was stopped at $39,490. Since then, bitcoin has dipped 7.3% during the early morning (EST) trading sessions on Friday.</strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    Bitcoin $40K Attempt Stopped Short, Crypto Prices Remain Range-Bound
  </h2>
  
  <ul>
    <li>
      Bitcoin (BTC) is down today after trying to surpass the psychological $40,000 region but was stopped short. BTC is down more than 7.3% today and is currently swapping for $35,890 per unit.
    </li>
    <li>
      The leading crypto asset BTC lost some steam after Elon Musk tweeted about the digital currency on Twitter by sharing some memes and a broken heart emoji.
    </li>
  </ul><figure id="attachment_463879" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-463879" style="width: 2428px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-463879 size-full" title="Crypto Consolidation Continues — Bitcoin's Attempt to Rise Above Psychological Levels Falls Short" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/bitstamp_btc_usd-fri_4_jun_07_55_05.jpg" alt="Crypto Consolidation Continues — Bitcoin's Attempt to Rise Above Psychological Levels Falls Short" width="2428" height="1316" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/bitstamp_btc_usd-fri_4_jun_07_55_05.jpg 2428w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/bitstamp_btc_usd-fri_4_jun_07_55_05-300x163.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/bitstamp_btc_usd-fri_4_jun_07_55_05-1024x555.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/bitstamp_btc_usd-fri_4_jun_07_55_05-768x416.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/bitstamp_btc_usd-fri_4_jun_07_55_05-1536x833.jpg 1536w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/bitstamp_btc_usd-fri_4_jun_07_55_05-2048x1110.jpg 2048w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/bitstamp_btc_usd-fri_4_jun_07_55_05-696x377.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/bitstamp_btc_usd-fri_4_jun_07_55_05-1392x754.jpg 1392w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/bitstamp_btc_usd-fri_4_jun_07_55_05-1068x579.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/bitstamp_btc_usd-fri_4_jun_07_55_05-775x420.jpg 775w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/bitstamp_btc_usd-fri_4_jun_07_55_05-1920x1041.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2428px) 100vw, 2428px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-463879" class="wp-caption-text">BTC/USD on Friday, June 4, 2021.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <ul>
    <li>
      30 day stats show BTC is down 36% while three-month stats show bitcoin (BTC) has lost over 25%. The leading crypto asset’s all-time high above the $64k handle took place around two months ago.
    </li>
  </ul><figure id="attachment_463878" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-463878" style="width: 2428px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
